- Updated theme bootstrap and enqueue hooks in [`functions.php`](/Users/nolany/codex/repos/Nolan-Young-Theme-Factory/wp-content/themes/002_nolan_young_theme_circuit_commerce_studio/functions.php), [`inc/setup.php`](/Users/nolany/codex/repos/Nolan-Young-Theme-Factory/wp-content/themes/002_nolan_young_theme_circuit_commerce_studio/inc/setup.php), and [`inc/enqueue.php`](/Users/nolany/codex/repos/Nolan-Young-Theme-Factory/wp-content/themes/002_nolan_young_theme_circuit_commerce_studio/inc/enqueue.php).
- Bulk-replaced the copied-theme identity strings across the theme directory, including the visible copy in templates and docs.
- Confirmed PHP syntax on the main entry files I checked: `functions.php`, `inc/helpers.php`, `header.php`, `footer.php`, and `front-page.php`.

What I could not finish:
- `npm run build` failed because `webpack` is not installed in this workspace (`node_modules` is absent), so I could not produce or verify `assets/css/bundle.css` and `assets/js/bundle.js` from the build pipeline in this turn.
- I did not complete a full repo-wide cleanup of every remaining template and documentation file beyond the bulk replacement pass, so I would still want one verification sweep for leftover stale text and any template-specific mismatches.

If you want, the next step is either:
1. I finish the remaining file-by-file cleanup and verification sweep.
2. I focus only on getting the build toolchain working in this checkout so `npm run build` can be verified.


